<<~ ahu slot=`#/forks`>>

!! Forks (moʻolelo, overrulable)
# ''Lift input:'' the door takes `{title, digest}` and no body at all, so a hand cannot even pass one. The alternative was keeping `text` and checking it against the row.
# ''Digest:'' content digest over body plus carried fields (a field change moves it). Proposals keep their body digest, checked against the staged text.
# ''Signing the digest:'' the digest rides as a `staged:<digest>` source, so I did not change the mesh lift act schema.
# ''Check order:'' the staged-row check runs before the cap and grant, so an unstaged lift opens no root.
# ''Re-lifts:'' import and seed re-lifts stage first, then lift. They keep the typed count as their eyes, and add no bypass row.
# ''Staging is open to seats:'' `kahua-stage` is seat-allowed, matching the two-tier law "AI promotes, unsigned".
# ''Confirm:'' typing back the first 8 hex at a TTY, or `--digest` (the full digest) in scripts.
# ''Browser label location:'' OPFS at the node's relative path, rather than a new export record.
# ''Gate:'' a ratchet with per-package ceilings, not report-only and not red.

